=== 3. The one device with headroom (emulator-5560, 2158892KB / ~64% used) is occupied by another live session ===
qa_lock_survey flags it occupied_without_lock=yes (excluded from effective_capacity).
Corroborating host-side evidence (per NEARS memory: device-hold-needs-host-process-not-pidof — ps naming the serial is the only valid proof):
  $ ps aux | grep 5560
  Apple  38514  ... /Users/Apple/Library/Android/sdk/platform-tools/adb -s emulator-5560 shell -x logcat -v time -T '08-30 06:35:36.705'
A live adb logcat tail process is attached to this serial from outside this session — treated as a live occupant per the survey's own computation and per the shared-tree concurrency rules; not taken over.

=== 4. Spare-AVD escalation checked (NEARS-2489 "boot a spare before queueing") ===
$ emulator -list-avds
NEARS_2411_QA, NEARS_2414_QA, NEARS_2424_QA, Pixel_10_Pro, Pixel_10_Pro_2, Pixel_10_Pro_3, nears_qa_delivery, nears_qa_wave56
Mapped every currently-booted serial to its AVD name (adb -s <serial> emu avd name) — all 8 listed AVDs are already booted as the 8 running emulator- serials above. No spare AVD exists to boot fresh (which would have started with a clean/larger free-space image).

=== Conclusion ===
Every device in the Android pool is either below the 800MB disk floor (post one-reclaim-attempt-each, per protocol's "never loop it" rule) or genuinely held by another live session. No spare capacity exists. Per workflow-profile: "still below ... → report LOW DISK ... and try the next pool device (or return BLOCKED{queue: ...} if the whole platform pool is low-disk/locked)" — this is that state, for the entire pool, not a single device.
AC3 (live regression + combined-screen-load) and the live component of AC1/AC2 (network interception on a real device) could NOT be demonstrated on-device this pass. AC1/AC2 are instead evidenced via the automated backstop + independent falsifiability re-check (see ac1-ac2-automated-falsifiability.log), as pre-authorized by the QA Test Scope note for this ticket. AC3's regression-of-existing-behavior claim is additionally supported statically (controller/screen code paths reviewed, see the same log) and by the still-passing "non-empty transaction list" test cases, but this is NOT a substitute for the live device confirmation the scope asked for — reported as BLOCKED, not PASS, on that AC.
